## Improvements

- [GLOBAL] **Large single `Write` calls kill the connection.** The prompt-creator died twice with `API Error: Connection lost before a response was produced`, both times at the moment of emitting a ~17 KB file write, producing zero files. Instructing it to write incrementally (Write frontmatter+`<summary>`, then Edit to append each section, ≤~4 KB per call) made it succeed immediately. This should be a standing rule in the prompt-creator agent definition for any multi-prompt generation, since 15–20 KB prompt files are the normal output size — the failure is silent (no file, no error artifact) and costs a full ~15-minute context-rebuild per retry.
- [GLOBAL] **A resumed agent is not a retried agent.** `SendMessage` to a failed agent's ID preserves its context, so the two failures cost ~30 minutes of re-exploration only because I did not resume after the first one. Worth stating in the run-prompt / generate-prompts command docs: on a subagent API error, resume by ID rather than re-invoking.
- [GUIDE] `dark-factory:prompt-auditor` should state the grep dialect it assumes. Audit 3's Critical finding hinges on `grep -q <pattern> <dir>` recursing under **ugrep 7.8.4** (this image) versus erroring under GNU grep — a verification line that fails on one and vacuously passes on the other. The auditor did verify this on the image, which is exactly right, but the guide should make "confirm the image's grep dialect before scoring a directory-targeted grep" an explicit step so it is not rediscovered per run.
- [PROMPT] The generated prompts carry `branch:` in the inbox frontmatter, which all three auditors flagged as outside the DoD's allowed set (`spec`, `status`, `created`, `issue`). The spec-001 prompts carry it too, so the generator emits it consistently — either the DoD should list `branch` as allowed or the generator should stop emitting it. Currently it produces a finding on every single audit, which is noise.
- [GUIDE] The Ginkgo suite-file boilerplate (`time.Local = time.UTC`, `format.TruncatedDiff = false`, 60 s suite timeout, `RunSpecs`) is now duplicated across `pkg/scripts`, `pkg/factory`, `pkg/prompts` and `pkg/verdict`. Spec 001's prompt inlined it verbatim; spec 002's prompts reference `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` as the shape instead. A short `go-ginkgo-suite-file.md` in the coding docs would remove the last reason to inline it and make the two specs' prompts consistent.
- [PROMPT] `docs/verdict-gate.md` is described in prompt 1 as carrying the reason strings "verbatim", but the pinned per-rule message formats for rules a, b, d, e, g and i exist only in the prompt. The spec says "A rule change updates that page in the same change", so the page should carry the exact strings — otherwise the next rule change has to diff a prompt to find them. | duration: 660677ms | cost: $17.2601 | tokens: 261 in / 7873 out
